{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1388739-journey-to-the-west","id":1388739,"title":"Journey to the West","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-15T12:54:04-07:00","id":1388739,"title":"Journey to the West","content":"Hello.<br /> <br /> With the arrival of Fangs at the Gate, I decided to do a little mental stretch and see if I could recreate the group from Journey to the West (not the original, one I saw in a manwha) as Exalted. <br /> <br /> Most of the cast (excluded the horse) can be written as Lunar pretty easily. With a little stretch of the imagination, you can also give everyone else a different Caste without duplicates. Sun Wukong can be a Changing Moon (because it's a trickster, even if his martial power is what usually is noticed more), Pigsy can be a Full Moon (because... he's doesn't really do a lot aside fro fighting), and the Sand Demon can be a No Moon (maybe the Sand is because he was a God-Blooded? Or maybe some Eclipse Charms he got using Lunar sorcery. Both works). A little stretchy but doable, as they're pretty faithful to the original source.<br /> <br /> The horse is really a dragon so he's excluded, but he could be a Castless Lunar if you really want to squeeze it.<br /> <br /> Then I hit a wall with Tang Sazang. <br /> <br /> In the Manwha Tang Sazang is just a little different from the original. It's implied that he has basically the same background... with the difference that he can also kick your ass using martial arts and possesses Buddhistic Techniques to purify and destroy corrupted spirits... mainly by emitting waves of golden light and puncturing weak points in the defense of the opponent. Basically Golden Jannissary + Solar Brawl for when he has to grapple someone or the opponent is not a monster + whatever Solar mumbo jumbo taken from other skills. And Snake Style if you want to go for 'hit the weak point', but it could simply be stunting.<br /> <br /> Aside from that he knows everything both mundane and supernatural, it's capable of healing almost anything using acupuncture, knows every important person everywhere and he's a master negotiator and diplomat. Or at least he seems pretty used to calm down angry supernatural critters and make them talk instead of kill and knows a lot of people thanks to his journey.<br /> <br /> And I have no idea what Caste use for him. I excluded Dawn and Night because the skill and themes are not aligned with him and the Anima owers too don't really mesh well with the character. Twilight could technically work skills-wise but the Anima effects are no good. He doesn't go around throwing forcefields and summoning elementals like Ash Ketchum.<br /> <br /> That leaves Eclipse and Zenith. Both have at least some skills that would be useful (Integrity, Lore, Presence, Resistance, and Athletics for the Zenith, Larceny, Linguistic, Occult, Socialize, and Presence/Bureaucracy/Ride for the Eclipse). The Eclipse is also thematically more fit for him since while he's good at talking he's not exactly some figure that demand respect and guide the masses by sheer charisma and passionate speeches like the -stereotypical, I admit- Zenith do, he's more like a diplomatic that try to de-escalate the situation. But that's a problem that's a fluff problem, not a mechanical one.<br /> <br /> So Eclipse is actually a good fit... except for the fact that he doesn't really use Eclipse Charms, but that can be hand-waved by him not finding Eclipse charms he would actually want to use. But Zenith Anima powers work well for fighting and all that 'I emit golden light to destroy you', but... maybe it's better to use Golden Janissary for that? I suck at remembering what Charms do.<br /> <br /> And since I already reached my limit regarding building this character and I'm curious how people with more knowledge of me on the matter would do, how would you build him? Zenith or Eclipse? Or something else? What Attributes and what Skills (I think he needs at least Dodge or Resistance, but maybe I'm wrong)? Tell me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T02:51:47-07:00","id":1388871,"title":"","content":"Sorry, is this a thought exercise or an actual game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T03:18:20-07:00","id":1388874,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t see anything wrong with his being an Integrity Supernal Zenith. It\u2019s not like there\u2019s a required minimum of dots one must invest in the Caste Abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T05:50:12-07:00","id":1388896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1388739-journey-to-the-west?p=1388871#post1388871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, is this a thought exercise or an actual game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thought excercise. Maybe I'll use him if I find a game, but right now I don't really have a group to play with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T07:06:24-07:00","id":1388925,"title":"","content":"Tripitaka as a <i>Zenith</i>, emphasizing him as a holy man: Integrity/Lore/Performance/Presence/Survival; Supernal Integrity or Presence.<br /> <br /> Tripitaka as a <i>Twilight</i>, emphasizing him as a teacher: Integrity/Linguistics/Lore/Medicine/Occult; Supernal Integrity.<br /> <br /> Tripitaka as an <i>Eclipse</i>, emphasizing him as a pilgrim: Linguistics/Occult/Presence/Ride/Socialize; Supernal Presence.<br /> <br /> Zenith probably accomplishes what you want the easiest, and would give you the most options, as a Zenith can take either Integrity (and thus the various meditation Charms) or Presence (for Enemy-Castigating Solar Judgement, Empowering Shout, and the Underling-Promoting Touch line of Charms).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T08:16:06-07:00","id":1388946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1388739-journey-to-the-west?p=1388925#post1388925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tripitaka as a <i>Zenith</i>, emphasizing him as a holy man: Integrity/Lore/Performance/Presence/Survival; Supernal Integrity or Presence.<br /> <br /> Tripitaka as a <i>Twilight</i>, emphasizing him as a teacher: Integrity/Linguistics/Lore/Medicine/Occult; Supernal Integrity.<br /> <br /> Tripitaka as an <i>Eclipse</i>, emphasizing him as a pilgrim: Linguistics/Occult/Presence/Ride/Socialize; Supernal Presence.<br /> <br /> Zenith probably accomplishes what you want the easiest, and would give you the most options, as a Zenith can take either Integrity (and thus the various meditation Charms) or Presence (for Enemy-Castigating Solar Judgement, Empowering Shout, and the Underling-Promoting Touch line of Charms).</div> </div> </div> </div>First thing: thank you for your answer.<br /> <br /> Second: since I'm not very good at remembering what Charms actually do, do Socialize is useful for a diplomat character, or it's overshadowed by Presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T08:26:10-07:00","id":1388948,"title":"","content":"Socialize is primarily useful for teasing out the motives of characters, hide your own motives, and perform influence during highly-formal social scenes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T08:35:55-07:00","id":1388952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1388739-journey-to-the-west?p=1388948#post1388948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Socialize is primarily useful for teasing out the motives of characters, hide your own motives, and perform influence during highly-formal social scenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, ok. So useful for a diplomat in a foreign court, not as much for one travelling around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T08:49:15-07:00","id":1388956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shapechanger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1388739-journey-to-the-west?p=1388952#post1388952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, ok. So useful for a diplomat in a foreign court, not as much for one travelling around.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, it will still be quite useful, as Guile and Read Intentions are cornerstones of the social system, and most Socialize Charms enhance or build off them in some way. Certain Charms (Mastery of Small Manners/Culture Hero Approach) are even <i>specifically</i> for dealing with unfamiliar cultures and customs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T09:12:57-07:00","id":1388962,"title":"","content":"It also helps you to know the customs of foreign\u2019s cultures which is useful for a traveler. And the ability to reflect any accusations at you back to the accuser would also be good for dealing with xenophobic folks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T09:20:44-07:00","id":1388966,"title":"","content":"I see. Mmmm... I'm not sure I can squeeze all the necessary Caste/Favoured skills there. This version is also a decent fighter... he needs at least some Brawl, Martial Arts and Dodge/Resistance to be decent in fights. <br /> <br /> Mmmm... maybe it's possible to not make Brawl Favored? I don't remember the various costs right away, but considering Solar Experience, maybe it's doable to not giving him Favoured combat skills? He can start with Dexterity 3 and Brawl/Martial Arts 3 and go from there. Considering the Excellency, it shouldn't be too difficult to match most critters in combat, considering he also has companions...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T11:16:12-07:00","id":1388996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shapechanger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1388739-journey-to-the-west?p=1388966#post1388966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. Mmmm... I'm not sure I can squeeze all the necessary Caste/Favoured skills there. This version is also a decent fighter... he needs at least some Brawl, Martial Arts and Dodge/Resistance to be decent in fights. <br /> <br /> Mmmm... maybe it's possible to not make Brawl Favored? I don't remember the various costs right away, but considering Solar Experience, maybe it's doable to not giving him Favoured combat skills? He can start with Dexterity 3 and Brawl/Martial Arts 3 and go from there. Considering the Excellency, it shouldn't be too difficult to match most critters in combat, considering he also has companions...</div> </div> </div> </div>That fits with the default expectations of the game (Manticore's are deadly foes the Exalted can defeat, bears are a good combat match for Dynasts, Nephwracks are boss villains, etc.).<br /> <br /> It doesn't necessarily fit with a mechanical optimisation approach to the game.<br /> <br /> So... sure, go for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T11:26:15-07:00","id":1389004,"title":"","content":"Well, I suppose it all depends on how much optimization you think it's fair for someone that's not a dedicated fighter. Sure, maybe the Lunar Sun Wukong can start with Dex 5 Brawl/Melee/Martial Arts 5 (but probably 3 because I'm a sucker for putting all Bonus point on Attributes for starting Lunars), because he's supposed to be a legendary fighter and all, but this guy is not supposed to be that good from the start. He can become a legendary fighter later.<br /> <br /> After all, this Manwha is actually a sequel of the original Journey, so it makes sense that he's not on par with the devilish powerful Lunar warrior from the start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}